    "content": [
      {
        "id": "industrial-role",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "From hydrocarbons to industrial materials",
        "content": "Petrochemicals connect oil and gas extraction with chemical manufacturing. A feedstock is material transformed into another product; fuel supplies energy for that transformation. The distinction matters because a petrochemical complex can require natural gas in both roles. The U.S. Energy Information Administration identifies petroleum products and natural gas as feedstocks for Iran’s petrochemical production. [s1]\n\nThis makes the industry different from a simple extension of crude-oil exports. Evaluating it requires asking what materials enter a plant, what products leave it, and which further manufacturing stages occur inside Iran. Iran Open Data’s analysis identifies a concentration in basic chemicals and limited downstream processing as structural weaknesses. That is an interpretation of the industry’s product mix, rather than proof that every producer has the same business model. [s2]",
